  "details": "I have a problem with hearing and understanding people in group settings. Either my earmuff settings are set very small and I can hear only the closest 2 or 3 people, or I make it slightly bigger and I can hear all the people around me at an equal volume. \n\nI understand how the settings work; red circle is full volume, and then white circle tapers off until the volume hits the outside voice volume setting. The problem is that the white circle is either very big and I hear too many people, or it is very small and the falloff range (volume 100% to 0%) all happens in that tiny sliver of space.\n\nI'm not sure if the falloff volume is linear with distance, or if it's exponential? I would love some way to adjust the curve of the falloff volume. That way I can still have a large white circle, but the volume drop off is much more aggressively exponential with distance. Right now there is just not enough difference between adjacent people and near-by people.\n\nI hope I'm explaining this well. \n\nThanks for taking the time to read this!\n\nAngst!",
